{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"A6-0a oracle card (strong-tier, pre-code): contract = signed epoch state matrix plus exact no-union/ref-preservation behavior. Preconditions = common-ancestor divergent refs; local/remote .store-compat records independently absent, epoch-absent, equal, mismatched, corrupt, or unreadable. Production paths = compat remote git-show reader -> sync._union_merge and push_tickets_branch non-FF retry; lower tiers cannot prove Git ref preservation or CLI logging. Unit postconditions = every matrix row, distinct absent-vs-unreadable result, valid-epoch preservation and non-string drop. Integration postconditions = exact local/remote tips unchanged, zero merge/re-push, WARNING emitted, fsck DIVERGED (never PUSH_PENDING), matching-epoch merge plus behind/ahead controls, real CLI stderr. Collateral invariants = no MERGE_HEAD, clean index, both event commits reachable; recovery = explicit re-clone/reset, not retry. Contention exemption: this adds no new check-then-act composition or retry/cache; it guards existing already-locked single merge seams. Surface census: CLI in scope via subprocess; library facade in scope via real write/push; MCP/API out of scope because it adds no distinct path after the shared core; automated review-bot caller out of scope here and receives a deployed-runtime probe in A6-0b; dual-direction in scope through separate sync and push oracles. Plan re-certified PASS at c1f1179b59. Advisory accepted: add the fourth non-string write_compat_record case and verify compound log/subprocess clauses separately."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785815488147591001,"uuid":"0cb70706-9615-4bfc-8b4a-9f7f20894da7"}